package server

const mcpParallelPolicy = " Explicit fork/join is supported in schemaVersion 1: fork nodes carry fork:{joinNodeId,branchEdgeIds}, join nodes carry join:{forkNodeId}. Every outgoing fork edge is a mandatory branch of the same original case, without type filters. All successful branches must reach their paired join before that case continues. Configure complete paired regions atomically with versioned PUT /diagrams/{diagramId}/simulation; isolated unpaired CRUD is rejected with structured validation issues. Limits: 2..64 branches, 16 nested pairs, no cycles or crossed/foreign incoming paths inside parallel regions. Shared resources and per-branch queues/costs are real; business populations/revenue count original cases once. Any branch failure/abandonment cancels its siblings, releases resources, preserves incurred costs and ends the case once. State.parallel exposes correlated group summaries and active/created/joined/cancelled branch counts. Join node metrics include join.waitingGroups,arrivedBranches,expectedBranches,completedGroups,cancelledGroups,wait; its queue counts arrived waiting tasks. Token lineage carries rootParticleId,parentParticleId,forkGroupId,forkNodeId,joinNodeId,branchEdgeId; waiting parents/children are not completed cases. Events include PARTICLE_FORKED,BRANCH_JOINED,JOIN_COMPLETED,BRANCH_CANCELLED,PROCESS_CANCELLED. Suspended parents and branch tokens share the 200000 active-token limit; samples/retention are distinct from full business metrics. Discover parallel-delivery-simulator through GET /templates for the three-branch Parallel SD-WAN delivery example with shared engineers, warehouse, one billing outcome and a paid capacity scenario."
